measured on (Spearman rank correlation).
\item Converting that rank back into the target event's raw units by
multiplying by the TARGET's \code{sigma_between} reintroduces the same
parametric assumption on the other side. Fixed by mapping the
(correlation-shrunk) implied percentile onto the target event's \emph{own
empirical} distribution of \code{ability_raw} (quantile-to-quantile).
\item Getting that empirical distribution from \code{ability} itself requires
every OTHER athlete's \code{ability_raw} in both events, which conflicts
with \verb{estimate_ability(only = <entrants>)}, the fast path every real
caller uses and that deliberately never computes that. Fixed by taking
the population reference as a separate, precomputed argument -- see
\code{\link[=build_neighbour_rank_reference]{build_neighbour_rank_reference()}} for how to build and cache one
cheaply.
