\code{rank_reference} to get its percentile, converted to a normal quantile
\code{z}, shrunk toward the target event's median by the correlation
(\code{sqrt(r2) * z}, standard regression-to-the-mean for two variables
correlated at \code{r}), turned back into a probability with \code{pnorm()}, and
that probability is looked up against the target event's row of
\code{rank_reference} to get an implied raw ability on the target's actual
scale. That implied value is blended into the athlete's own \code{ability_raw}
(from \code{ability}, not \code{rank_reference}) with weight \verb{r2 * (one race's worth of weight in the target event for this athlete)}, so a neighbour
